@startuml
title Showcase — browse products and view top customers
autonumber

actor "Admin / Staff / Customer" as User
boundary "Showcase Shop View" as View
control "Store Context" as Store
control "Supabase Client" as Supabase
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Load public shop data ==
activate Store
Store -> Supabase: Select products, categories and orders
activate Supabase
Supabase -> DB: Read showcase data
activate DB
DB --> Supabase: Product, category and order rows
deactivate DB
Supabase --> Store: Loaded records
deactivate Supabase
Store --> View: Current products, categories and orders
deactivate Store
View --> User: Display shop showcase

alt Browse clothing
  User -> View: Search, select category\nor set maximum price
  activate View
  View -> View: Filter products in memory
  View --> User: Display matching products
  deactivate View
else View top customers
  User -> View: Select month or custom date range
  activate View
  View -> View: Group sales by customer name,\nincluding walk-in sales
  View -> View: Sort by spend and keep top 10
  View --> User: Display ranked customers
  deactivate View
end

opt Product or order data changes
  DB -> Supabase: PostgreSQL change event
  activate Supabase
  Supabase -> Store: Reload changed table
  activate Store
  Store --> View: Updated showcase data
  deactivate Store
  deactivate Supabase
  activate View
  View -> View: Reapply current search or customer filters
  View --> User: Refresh displayed results
  deactivate View
end
@enduml
  